On Sun, 17 Dec 2006, Christian wrote:
>
> I've been trying to compile nethack so that I can start using some of
> the patches I've read about.  Anyway,  I got the source without
> difficulties.  I got DJGPP and got it installed properly including the
> path and environment settings.  I've followed all of the instructions
> in install.dos and every suggestion I've found in the usenet groups,
> but no one has mentioned the problem I'm having.  It is most likely
> something unbelievably easy, but I can't figure it out.  When I type
> "make install" in the \src directory I get the following message:
> C:\dev\nh343\src>make install
> make.exe: *** No rule to make target `install'.  Stop.

   Two ideas: First, the makefile should be named "Makefile", not
"makefile". This makes a difference to some Windows programs; I forget
whether DJGPP cares.
   Second, are you sure that typing "make" invokes the DJGPP make
utility, or could it be trying to run some other "make.exe" earlier
in your PATH? This probably isn't the answer; but you can make sure
by typing "c:\djgpp\bin\make.exe" (or whatever) instead of just "make".

   Also, there's no reason to say "install" explicitly. Invoking "make"
with no command-line arguments should work just as well, if not better.
(However, first you need to get 'make' to find the Makefile, yeah.)

